as become an essential resource for understanding societal trends in the United States and beyond. Key figures associated with its establishment include Andrew Kohut, who served as its founding director, and the broader Pew Charitable Trusts, which provided the initial funding and vision for the Center. Its significance lies in its ability to synthesize vast amounts of information to inform public policy, business strategy, and civic discourse.

